From 0b9e77ff47e3eb0a7d502da57237fac1da8903bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: equuleus port <port@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sdm845-common: allow ParanoidSense to open the aux IR camera

frameworks/base Camera.shouldExposeAuxCamera() collapses enumeration to two
cameras for any package not listed in vendor.camera.aux.packagelist:

    String packageName = ActivityThread.currentOpPackageName();
    List<String> packageList = Arrays.asList(
        SystemProperties.get("vendor.camera.aux.packagelist", packageName).split(","));
    ...
    return packageList.contains(packageName) && !packageExcludelist.contains(packageName);

The IR camera is an auxiliary device, so a correct camera id alone is not
enough: without co.aospa.sense in this list the app still cannot open it.

This APPENDS to the existing list. A widely-copied adaptation of this change
replaces org.lineageos.aperture.dev with co.aospa.sense; doing that here would
silently remove Aperture's auxiliary-camera access, so every existing entry is
preserved verbatim and the new package is appended.
---
diff --git a/vendor.prop b/vendor.prop
index 8a741d7..cac9e38 100644
--- a/vendor.prop
+++ b/vendor.prop
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ persist.vendor.qcom.bluetooth.twsp_state.enabled=false
 vendor.qcom.bluetooth.soc=cherokee
 
 # Camera
-vendor.camera.aux.packagelist=com.android.camera,org.codeaurora.snapcam,org.lineageos.aperture,org.lineageos.aperture.dev
+vendor.camera.aux.packagelist=com.android.camera,org.codeaurora.snapcam,org.lineageos.aperture,org.lineageos.aperture.dev,co.aospa.sense
 
 # Chipset
 ro.soc.manufacturer=Qualcomm
